spoint client/AnimationStateMachine.js: the REAL root cause of 'holding shift never reaches SprintLoop' (after thresholds were already coupled to sprintSpeed per anim-locostate-thresholds-vs-sprintspeed) is a sendLoco/xstate-actor desync. sendLoco did actor.send(event) FIRST then transitionTo(actor value); when transitionTo bailed on the LOCO_COOLDOWN (0.3s) loco->loco guard, the actor had ALREADY advanced (e.g. to SprintLoop) while the visual `current` stayed JogFwdLoop. The actor has no SPRINT self-transition, so resolveLocoEvent (using stale current=Jog) kept emitting SPRINT but snap.can('SPRINT') was false from the already-Sprint actor -> event dropped forever -> stuck on Jog. FIX: a static LOCO_EVENT_TARGET map (WALK->WalkLoop, JOG->JogFwdLoop, SPRINT->SprintLoop, CROUCH_FWD->CrouchFwdLoop, plus idles) lets sendLoco test the shared locoSwapBlocked(target) guard BEFORE actor.send, keeping actor and current in lockstep so the swap retries once cooldown clears. NOTE xstate5 snapshot.machine.transition(snap,event) THROWS 'Cannot read actionExecutor' as a peek - do not use it; derive the target from the event instead. Second fix same file: walk/loco timeScale 'wrong speed on re-press' - smoothTimeScale/smoothSpeed persisted across idle (frozen, sometimes negative); on fresh entry into a moving loco state (tracked via scaledLocoState, cleared to null on Jump/Land/Death one-shots) snap smoothSpeed=live speed and smoothTimeScale=signedTarget so cadence is proportional from frame one; sustained-state changes still lerp. Browser-witnessed live Idle->Jog->SprintLoop at speed 12, timeScale proportional. window.__animProbe (local animator getDebug) added to client/app.js tickPlayerAnimators for witness; local anim.update wrapped in try/catch (errors -> window.__animErr) so a per-frame anim throw can't kill the render loop. Committed 6bfb4a9f.